\"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0fd17e64d147dc97c0d9615a62b27cbd81272baccb71dc442aa38286c3f7e1df","event_uuid":"25400faa-67ea-4e62-b8e2-c5156210dece","position":{"commit_sha":"730febfb680874932c9747a5c1619eb9ec2adb4a","position":"1788813794439029001-25400faa-67ea-4e62-b8e2-c5156210dece"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0e9ae43405f147a254218b8e3be71ba8c6be5a0b3e998ef79d7a87b131587d05","event_uuid":"68b32cf7-b502-4bc1-9978-2836a0831fc0","position":{"commit_sha":"a4ec6c94ea59529bf21987ef549ed3b240f09b64","position":"1788814649318893001-68b32cf7-b502-4bc1-9978-2836a0831fc0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"afd88e64f063ac2caf3f48ce11c4c266efe61251cee7b472df3af359769c066a","event_uuid":"fc4885d2-bdf3-4bb1-9a75-9fd4efba2d5c","position":{"commit_sha":"420c16d13ffa32f783030fe000c71943ae78dd44","position":"1788815035586703001-fc4885d2-bdf3-4bb1-9a75-9fd4efba2d5c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dbbae60fa50823e74cc775bcdafd622e5bf7d197e296d1733dd744d39dcc0203","event_uuid":"2869b543-32b1-4cb7-a949-771a2a5abff2","position":{"commit_sha":"658f4a3dc1230f9c3cabea209967b10477ab33cb","position":"1788815044828290001-2869b543-32b1-4cb7-a949-771a2a5abff2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation progress: reproduced the no-common-ancestor tracker split in a regression test. The first attempted comment now refuses before creating a new local commit, preserving the previous HEAD. Confirmed make worktree does not create an independent tracker clone in the normal path: linked code worktrees symlink .tickets-tracker to the main worktree's shared tracker. Documented that fsck-recover preserves dangling ticket commits from stale rebase/merge recovery, but unrelated live local histories require isolated operator recovery/tracker-maintenance while other writers are quiesced.","timestamp":1788800117410426001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788589242474082001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4daa958a-c1db-46f2-9887-2e127ea48867","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6963-2dae-c21f-435e"},{"link_uuid":"3f7f5492-e415-46ed-9d63-46bc7378deb0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a67b-7370-d19d-4153"}],"description":"## What is confirmed\n\nAn agent's ticket writes were **lost** and survived only because it also described them in its\nprose report. Specifically, on `torrential-unwhite-snail` (`9c2e-b44c-119e-4105`) the agent:\n\n- retitled the ticket and raised it to priority 2, and\n- posted a root-cause comment containing a fully reproduced diagnosis (the four-xdist-workers /\n  four-gate-slots exhaustion, with a serial-vs-parallel experiment).\n\nNeither reached the shared store. Verified directly afterwards: the ticket was still **priority 3\nwith 1 comment**, its original state. The finding was recoverable only because I could re-derive it\nfrom the agent's report text and re-verify its three load-bearing facts against `origin/main`\nmyself.\n\nThat is a data-loss path through the shared record. The next agent to hit it may not restate its\nfindings in prose, and then the work is simply gone.\n\n## The reported mechanism — RELAYED, and NOT currently reproducible\n\nThe agent reported that its worktree's ticket-store clone had diverged from `origin/tickets` with\n**no shared history**, `rebar fsck` saying *\"The local store was built independently of the remote\n... its writes will never push\"*, and **2,492 unpushed commits across 142 distinct tickets**.\n\nI could not reproduce this. Checking three agent worktrees minutes later:\n\n    fix-acli-ceiling-partition        in sync      <- the very worktree that reported divergence\n    bug-9c93-ad8d-user-data-mounts    in sync\n    fix-b2ff-mcp-readonly-empty       ahead/behind (shared history, normal)\n\nand the shared store on the main checkout was `local HEAD == origin/tickets`, with `rebar fsck`\nreporting **no divergence line at all**. So the condition was transient and had healed by the time\nI looked. The 2,492/142 figures are the agent's measurement, not mine, and I am recording them as\nrelayed rather than established.\n\n## The one thing that worked, worth preserving\n\nThe failure was **loud at the end**: the agent's final two writes were REFUSED, with `fsck` naming\nthe condition and the remedy. That is why the agent noticed at all. Whatever the fix, keep that —\na silent local-only accumulation would be far worse than a refusal.\n\nBut note the asymmetry that produced the loss: writes made BEFORE the refusal appeared to succeed\nlocally and were stranded silently. Only the last two were refused. So \"loud on refusal\" is not the\nsame as \"loud on divergence\".\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Reproduce the divergence deliberately in a scratch worktree, or establish that it cannot\n      recur and say why. This ticket rests on a relayed observation; the first job is to make it\n      first-hand or refute it. A refutation is a valid outcome — close it as `not_a_bug` with the\n      evidence.\n- [x] Determine whether a worktree created by `make worktree` gets its own tracker clone, and\n      whether that clone can be built independently of the remote (the `fsck` text and the\n      `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` note both point at a re-clone that did not carry `.env-id` /\n      `.opcert-key` / `.ensure-applied`).\n- [x] A store that CANNOT push is detected at the first write, not the last. Proven by driving a\n      write against a deliberately-diverged clone and observing the refusal on write #1.\n- [x] If stranded commits are recoverable, the recovery path is documented and does not require an\n      operator to reconstruct findings from an agent's prose. `rebar fsck-recover` exists but is\n      mutating; establish whether it preserves stranded events or discards them, because those are\n      very different remedies when 142 tickets' worth of another session's work is involved.\n- [x] The interaction with concurrent sessions is stated: this host runs eleven worktrees against\n      one shared `tickets` branch, and any recovery that rewrites shared history is unsafe while\n      others are writing.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"summarize no-common-ancestor DIVERGED write refusal"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"document first-write DIVERGED refusal, recovery limits, concurrent-session safety"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/freshness.py","reason":"add no-common-ancestor write publishability probe"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"refuse ticket-event writes before committing into unpublishable store"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py","reason":"regression proving first write refuses on unrelated diverged store"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py","reason":"coverage for non-blocking write-probe branches"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6963-2dae-c21f-435e"],["relates_to","a67b-7370-d19d-4153"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"fc4885d2-bdf3-4bb1-9a75-9fd4efba2d5c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2d52-5abe-abb8-44ab","ticket_type":"bug","title":"An agent's ticket writes were stranded and lost: a retitle and a fully-reproduced root-cause comment never reached the shared store, recoverable only from the agent's prose report","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["24d11aec-c75d-49b6-bc47-8c25e01528ea","84e00451-823c-4c27-9d29-2ca6de0c8ce9","cb623c91-3eba-4c84-b3fb-dec170dbe040","b41957cc-66fc-41cb-a01f-d5340eafdf09","cca22ddb-737f-4e1b-b69c-9dffc7b52edb","4daa958a-c1db-46f2-9887-2e127ea48867","3f7f5492-e415-46ed-9d63-46bc7378deb0","cef114d5-81eb-43f0-b30a-e93a9247c196","25400faa-67ea-4e62-b8e2-c5156210dece","68b32cf7-b502-4bc1-9978-2836a0831fc0","fc4885d2-bdf3-4bb1-9a75-9fd4efba2d5c","2869b543-32b1-4cb7-a949-771a2a5abff2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788821912463760001,"uuid":"13cc3ddb-eab5-41bf-bab7-497b9fb530bd"}